1
00:00:04,500 --> 00:00:09,147
The End Narancia, when you get a sec,
let me see that key I risked my life for.

2
00:00:09,680 --> 00:00:10,510
Huh? Here.

3
00:00:10,760 --> 00:00:11,878
No, don't throw it!

4
00:00:13,560 --> 00:00:14,390
AHHHHH!

5
00:00:14,473 --> 00:00:15,303
That hurt, dumbass!

6
00:00:15,386 --> 00:00:16,908
You are such a drama queen.

7
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:20,697
I'd be happy my hand had feeling it
all given what you just went through.

8
00:00:20,780 --> 00:00:24,617
The damn thing has only been
reattached for 30 minutes, you idiot.

9
00:00:24,700 --> 00:00:26,840
So happy or not, it still hurts.

10
00:00:27,040 --> 00:00:28,500
But enough about that.

11
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:34,257
You safeguarded my daughter's life,
and therefore you have my gratitude.

12
00:00:34,340 --> 00:00:36,120
Go to Napoli Cinderella,

13
00:00:36,420 --> 00:00:40,596
Benario 6, look for the turtle at
the water fountain, and use this key.

14
00:00:40,980 --> 00:00:43,580
You are to take her to Venice by train.

15
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:48,620
Postscript says, directives will
cease once we've arrived in Venice.

16
00:00:48,900 --> 00:00:51,937
What the hell are we supposed
to find at this water fountain?

17
00:00:52,020 --> 00:00:56,177
Don't know, but the boss said there was
a way to travel under the enemy's radar.

18
00:00:56,260 --> 00:00:59,117
It'll be risky, but we have to trust him.

19
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:01,957
Speaking of the boss, do you
think he's maybe already there?

20
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:03,757
I mean, it kind of sounds like it.

21
00:01:03,840 --> 00:01:05,252
That doesn't concern us.

22
00:01:05,420 --> 00:01:07,655
Our focus is on finishing the mission.

23
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:12,157
There's a train bound for France in
ten minutes that we don't want to miss.

24
00:01:12,240 --> 00:01:13,460
Mista, we alone?

25
00:01:13,820 --> 00:01:15,957
Looks like we're in the clear for now.

26
00:01:16,040 --> 00:01:18,099
Once we get to the station, though,

27
00:01:18,240 --> 00:01:21,711
I bet the place will be swarming
with rats ready to snitch.

28
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:25,645
I can't imagine what you
must be going through.

29
00:01:25,960 --> 00:01:28,257
suddenly having a target
on your back because

30
00:01:28,340 --> 00:01:31,337
of an estranged father
it must be terrifying

31
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:36,797
oh i feel you fugo i've
been preoccupied by our

32
00:01:36,880 --> 00:01:39,586
lively new friends too
if you know what i mean

33
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:46,140
no that's not what i

34
00:01:52,680 --> 00:01:54,557
Please, miss, you gotta forget Fugo!

35
00:01:54,640 --> 00:01:57,037
He didn't mean to come off
as an over-eager horndog!

36
00:01:57,120 --> 00:01:59,037
I know it seems like
we hit the brakes so my

37
00:01:59,120 --> 00:02:01,197
man here could peek at
those jaunty jiggle sacks,

38
00:02:01,280 --> 00:02:03,417
but I give you my word that's not it!

39
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:05,117
Blame his weakness in the face of Fugo!

40
00:02:05,200 --> 00:02:06,030
Just shut up, would ya?

41
00:02:06,113 --> 00:02:07,377
I was bracing for impact,

42
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:09,877
and you're making it sound like
I was trying to cop a veal!

43
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:13,313
Just promise me whatever you
do, you won't tell the boss!

44
00:02:26,940 --> 00:02:29,740
Thank you.

45
00:04:03,400 --> 00:04:04,520
There he is.

46
00:04:05,020 --> 00:04:06,220
It's Bucciarati.

47
00:04:06,640 --> 00:04:08,280
I don't believe it.

48
00:04:08,420 --> 00:04:11,997
The dumbass actually showed up
to the station in broad daylight.

49
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,300
He'll regret that.

50
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:18,877
Maybe the pressure he's under has
made logic give way to desperation.

51
00:04:18,960 --> 00:04:23,607
Or perhaps the Stronzo thinks he's figured
out a way to throw us off the trail.

52
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:25,800
I'll still butcher him!

53
00:04:26,020 --> 00:04:29,940
He killed Illuso and Formaggio!
He's dead! Hey, moron!

54
00:04:30,740 --> 00:04:33,337
Cool it with this stupid
butcher crap, you hear me?

55
00:04:33,420 --> 00:04:35,420
It's annoying as all hell. Huh?

56
00:04:36,120 --> 00:04:39,560
Our squadra of mafiosi has
no need for talk like that.

57
00:04:40,240 --> 00:04:42,400
Leave that drivel to the weaklings.

58
00:04:42,940 --> 00:04:45,175
Our group has a peculiar way about us.

59
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:48,497
By the time primitive thoughts
like that enter our minds,

60
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:50,639
the enemy's already been butchered.

61
00:04:50,780 --> 00:04:53,057
There's no need to
announce the inevitable.

62
00:04:53,140 --> 00:04:55,375
Such words have never crossed my lips.

63
00:04:55,580 --> 00:04:58,080
Pesci, you need to follow my example.

64
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:00,047
Prove that you're one of us.

65
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:01,600
You understand.

66
00:05:02,320 --> 00:05:03,860
Well, do ya?

67
00:05:05,680 --> 00:05:06,540
I do.

68
00:05:06,720 --> 00:05:07,780
I got it, big bro.

69
00:05:08,760 --> 00:05:11,878
Say butchered from now on
like the job's a done deal.

70
00:05:12,900 --> 00:05:13,730
prosciutto

71
00:05:14,940 --> 00:05:15,770
Listen,

72
00:05:15,853 --> 00:05:19,037
I'll head over on the
platform here pesci you get

73
00:05:19,120 --> 00:05:22,300
on and head to the front
car from the inside on it

74
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:24,540
We'll corner him

75
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:27,800
We need the boss's daughter alive

76
00:05:36,180 --> 00:05:39,945
Bucciarati it's getting close to
departure time something wrong.

77
00:05:40,220 --> 00:05:43,720
This is the only water fountain
here I'm sure about that.

78
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:47,736
But there's no way this was
designed for this keyhole.

79
00:05:48,020 --> 00:05:49,240
And look at this.

80
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:52,017
You don't even need a key to open it.

81
00:05:52,100 --> 00:05:54,394
It's nothing more than an access hatch.

82
00:05:56,320 --> 00:05:59,438
Bucciarati, what about the
lock on that fire hydrant?

83
00:06:01,160 --> 00:06:03,980
This lock isn't a match either. Merda!

84
00:06:04,320 --> 00:06:07,177
How can this be the right place
if the key won't fit anywhere?

85
00:06:07,260 --> 00:06:08,380
This is maddening!

86
00:06:14,240 --> 00:06:15,937
Should we pass on this train?

87
00:06:16,020 --> 00:06:18,457
The train in 15 minutes is bound for Rome.

88
00:06:18,540 --> 00:06:19,370
Not a chance.

89
00:06:19,453 --> 00:06:22,477
The enemy probably knows we're
here and are headed to the station.

90
00:06:22,560 --> 00:06:24,736
We can't stay longer than we have to.

91
00:06:25,140 --> 00:06:25,970
Benario 6.

92
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:27,637
The turtle by the fountain.

93
00:06:27,720 --> 00:06:29,997
If this isn't the spot, then where is it?

94
00:06:30,080 --> 00:06:31,420
Damn it! What now?

95
00:06:36,980 --> 00:06:37,940
The turtle.

96
00:06:55,892 --> 00:06:56,722
Huh?

97
00:06:56,805 --> 00:06:57,635
Explain, Pesci.

98
00:06:57,718 --> 00:06:59,940
What the hell are you doing here? Huh?

99
00:07:00,160 --> 00:07:01,957
What are you doing here, big bro?

100
00:07:02,040 --> 00:07:03,922
Where did Bucciarati run off to?

101
00:07:12,460 --> 00:07:15,657
I know I saw him climb aboard
the train right before I did.

102
00:07:15,740 --> 00:07:19,457
And there's no way in hell you didn't pass
by him as he was walking down the aisle.

103
00:07:19,540 --> 00:07:21,180
Well, I'm right, aren't I?

104
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:24,089
You gotta believe me,
I didn't see nothing!

105
00:07:24,260 --> 00:07:26,460
Not Bucciarati, his annoying friends,

106
00:07:26,660 --> 00:07:30,000
that new guy, not even the
boss's twerp, none of them!

107
00:07:31,900 --> 00:07:34,665
This little disappearing
act doesn't sit right.

108
00:07:36,500 --> 00:07:38,794
The train's about to take off, big bro.

109
00:07:39,040 --> 00:07:41,317
They've got to be sneaking
around the station somewhere.

110
00:07:41,400 --> 00:07:42,680
They just gotta be.

111
00:07:42,960 --> 00:07:44,417
They don't know who's after them,

112
00:07:44,500 --> 00:07:48,117
so they're waiting to spot us
before hopping on a getaway train.

113
00:07:48,200 --> 00:07:50,435
I'm positive I'm not imagining things.

114
00:07:50,980 --> 00:07:53,509
There was something by
that water fountain.

115
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:56,000
He must have picked it up.

116
00:07:56,200 --> 00:07:59,917
He grabbed something dark by the
fountain before jumping on the train.

117
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:00,960
Pesci, get on!

118
00:08:01,640 --> 00:08:03,620
But why? Just do it!

119
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:05,457
I don't know how they're doing it,

120
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:07,177
but I have a hunch that Bucciarati and his

121
00:08:07,260 --> 00:08:09,077
little yes-men are
hiding out on this train.

122
00:08:09,160 --> 00:08:11,900
And you're basing all that on a hunch?

123
00:08:12,120 --> 00:08:15,377
The boss must be offering those
clots some kind of assistance.

124
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:17,217
We're gonna have to move quickly now.

125
00:08:17,300 --> 00:08:21,577
My hunch says this is the last chance
we're gonna have before we lose him.

126
00:08:21,660 --> 00:08:23,660
Stop gawking and get on the train!

127
00:08:25,840 --> 00:08:29,664
A three-and-a-half-hour train
ride separates Napoli from France.

128
00:08:30,860 --> 00:08:35,040
But the midway point, Roma, lies but
a mere one-and-a-half hours away.

129
00:08:37,940 --> 00:08:41,160
Oh, man, now we're stuck
on the train. Shut up.

130
00:08:43,220 --> 00:08:45,455
Pesci, there's a space under the door.

131
00:08:45,680 --> 00:08:47,940
Something must be back here. But what?

132
00:08:48,540 --> 00:08:51,337
Isn't that room for the
guy who drives the train?

133
00:08:51,420 --> 00:08:53,537
You really think seven
people could hole up

134
00:08:53,620 --> 00:08:55,237
in there without a single person noticing?

135
00:08:55,320 --> 00:08:56,220
That's crazy.

136
00:08:57,740 --> 00:08:59,080
Can't be too careful.

137
00:08:59,600 --> 00:09:02,247
Why don't you unleash
Fisherman and find out?

138
00:09:07,260 --> 00:09:08,260
Do it.

139
00:09:11,740 --> 00:09:12,570
Fisherman!

140
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:18,370
Hmm.

141
00:09:18,580 --> 00:09:22,480
Well, I'm not picking up on seven
assholes, but I do sense two.

142
00:09:23,920 --> 00:09:25,300
Come to papa.

143
00:09:32,400 --> 00:09:34,237
Merida, what a tight squeeze.

144
00:09:34,320 --> 00:09:38,137
only room for the engineer
no matter I know those

145
00:09:38,220 --> 00:09:42,297
bastards are somewhere on
this train huh hey wait just

146
00:09:42,380 --> 00:09:46,117
a second I only hooked
one of them what Gibbs I

147
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:48,377
could have sworn I heard
two hearts thumping in there

148
00:09:48,460 --> 00:09:51,817
so why'd my rod only
managed to hook the NG guy

149
00:09:51,900 --> 00:09:55,237
hey Pesci get off your ass
we're searching the train

150
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:58,177
from top to bottom we'll find
him and rip those cowards

151
00:09:58,260 --> 00:10:01,201
out from their hiding spot
but You're staying put.

152
00:10:01,940 --> 00:10:04,617
If Bucciarati's goons figure
out that we're here too,

153
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:07,237
you can bet they'll come
rushing in to stop the train.

154
00:10:07,320 --> 00:10:08,908
I got you covered, big bro.

155
00:10:09,200 --> 00:10:11,197
And don't forget about their cargo.

156
00:10:11,280 --> 00:10:15,097
As long as the girl's with them, they
can't tear through the train on a whim.

157
00:10:15,180 --> 00:10:16,709
They have to play it safe.

158
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:19,275
Which is what gives us the upper hand.

159
00:10:19,540 --> 00:10:23,775
We'll snatch the girl and off those
clowns before we reach Roma Termini!

160
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:31,557
the key wasn't made to
fit in a keyhole but

161
00:10:31,640 --> 00:10:34,228
it fit perfectly in the
shell of this turtle

162
00:10:35,220 --> 00:10:37,817
somehow that activated
the turtle's special

163
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:40,757
ability the key seems
to function as a portal

164
00:10:40,840 --> 00:10:43,417
to an alternate space
one where we can remain

165
00:10:43,500 --> 00:10:47,640
sight unseen so the turtle is a stand user

166
00:10:53,480 --> 00:10:54,557
Where am I?

167
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:55,700
Under a seat?

168
00:10:59,020 --> 00:10:59,850
Shit!

169
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,757
This place is the bomb diggity!

170
00:11:01,840 --> 00:11:04,075
This turtle's like a loungy spaceship!

171
00:11:04,500 --> 00:11:08,180
At first, I thought this room
was some sort of illusion.

172
00:11:08,620 --> 00:11:10,480
But it's a bonafide structure.

173
00:11:10,740 --> 00:11:12,800
And all the furniture is real, too.

174
00:11:13,160 --> 00:11:14,631
Even the drinks are cold.

175
00:11:15,500 --> 00:11:18,853
Perhaps the boss is responsible
for these accommodations.

176
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:23,118
For the most part, turtles will
remain quiet and still in dark spaces.

177
00:11:23,460 --> 00:11:27,519
In other words, we should be able
to travel to Venice without issue.

178
00:11:30,100 --> 00:11:30,930
Hmm.

179
00:11:31,013 --> 00:11:33,720
I guess hiding in here
would be pretty dumb, huh?

180
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:37,353
I wish my gut talked to me
the way that my big bros does.

181
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:49,500
Is Big Bro making this haze?

182
00:11:49,660 --> 00:11:50,780
Did you really?

183
00:11:53,260 --> 00:11:54,800
The thankful death!

184
00:11:56,800 --> 00:11:58,660
Bro, you're really doing it?

185
00:11:58,800 --> 00:12:01,137
And you're going to do
it to everybody on board?

186
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:03,277
We don't even know if
they're on this train.

187
00:12:03,360 --> 00:12:05,017
Shouldn't we figure that
out before we start?

188
00:12:05,100 --> 00:12:08,080
I told you, we're going
to be thorough about this.

189
00:12:08,660 --> 00:12:10,860
They're here all right, I know it.

190
00:12:11,420 --> 00:12:13,949
Besides, you're making
a fuss over nothing.

191
00:12:14,140 --> 00:12:18,457
Planes from all over fall from the sky
every year and the world keeps spinning.

192
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:20,600
These jumps are getting off easy.

193
00:12:49,740 --> 00:12:52,740
It's being stuck inside a
turtle has its drawbacks.

194
00:12:52,920 --> 00:12:54,038
It's kind of muggy.

195
00:12:54,800 --> 00:12:56,918
Hey, Narancia, you want a drink too?

196
00:12:57,940 --> 00:12:59,717
Hope you're good with it being cold.

197
00:12:59,800 --> 00:13:00,860
There's cola,

198
00:13:01,260 --> 00:13:06,140
and mineral water, sparkling water,
and apple, orange, and pineapple juice.

199
00:13:07,100 --> 00:13:09,218
Hey, are you listening to me at all?

200
00:13:10,300 --> 00:13:11,130
Huh?

201
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:12,711
You say something, Mista?

202
00:13:12,880 --> 00:13:15,197
I asked if you wanted something to drink.

203
00:13:15,280 --> 00:13:17,757
Though you might want to
try getting some shut-eye.

204
00:13:17,840 --> 00:13:19,557
You've seen better days there, man.

205
00:13:19,640 --> 00:13:22,217
I'll keep an eye on the
ceiling while you rest.

206
00:13:22,300 --> 00:13:23,480
Sounds like a plan.

207
00:13:24,220 --> 00:13:27,197
I'm actually starting to
feel a little achy anyway.

208
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:29,540
My back and shoulders are killing me.

209
00:13:29,800 --> 00:13:31,271
I think I'll cop a squat.

210
00:13:31,600 --> 00:13:34,482
Something warm would sure
hit the spot right now.

211
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:36,240
But nothing too heavy.

212
00:13:36,540 --> 00:13:39,457
For the last time, all we've
got in the fridge are cold ones.

213
00:13:39,540 --> 00:13:42,617
Come on, is your brain shut
down when you talk to people?

214
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:45,560
In that case, banana it is. Yeah.

215
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:50,780
Oh, gardens like these
really soothe the soul.

216
00:13:51,180 --> 00:13:53,280
Your stress just melts away.

217
00:13:53,980 --> 00:13:55,580
Ah, so heavenly.

218
00:13:56,260 --> 00:13:57,240
Man, oh man,

219
00:13:57,400 --> 00:13:59,837
what I'd give to bask in
that Garden of Eden's warm

220
00:13:59,920 --> 00:14:02,861
sunshine just daydreaming
about the good old days.

221
00:14:06,940 --> 00:14:09,100
Rose, would you cut that shit out?

222
00:14:09,260 --> 00:14:12,260
Nobody wants your nasty-ass
spit on the damn pages!

223
00:14:13,460 --> 00:14:14,290
Huh?

224
00:14:14,373 --> 00:14:15,397
You're saying I did what now?

225
00:14:15,480 --> 00:14:17,580
There's no way! You're crazy!

226
00:14:26,780 --> 00:14:29,309
You're, uh, drooling
pretty bad there, man.

227
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:31,060
That is so freaking nasty.

228
00:14:31,340 --> 00:14:32,760
The heck is that? Hey!

229
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:37,270
Huh?

230
00:14:37,980 --> 00:14:40,760
I was craving this
banana, but it's no good.

231
00:14:41,880 --> 00:14:43,520
I mean, just look at it.

232
00:14:43,660 --> 00:14:47,520
It's like a piece of old stale
beef jerky. That's funny.

233
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:49,457
You really had me going there.

234
00:14:49,540 --> 00:14:50,834
Good on you, Narancia.

235
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:53,277
Don't scare me like that.

236
00:14:53,360 --> 00:14:57,117
It almost looks like that thing coming
out of your mouth is a real tooth.

237
00:14:57,200 --> 00:15:00,977
I appreciate the commitment, but I
think you're taking the bit too far.

238
00:15:01,060 --> 00:15:03,472
Just what is that dangling thing made of?

239
00:15:05,120 --> 00:15:07,037
You say something again, mister?

240
00:15:07,120 --> 00:15:08,220
Speak louder.

241
00:15:09,320 --> 00:15:10,960
Stop whispering, would you?

242
00:15:11,140 --> 00:15:12,957
I can't hear what you're saying.

243
00:15:13,040 --> 00:15:16,569
These ears don't seem to be
working as well as they used to.

244
00:15:16,940 --> 00:15:19,317
Oh, and would you just
look at this banana?

245
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:20,920
It's falling apart.

246
00:15:21,680 --> 00:15:24,720
I can't eat something
like that! How gross!

247
00:15:26,620 --> 00:15:27,450
Disgusting!

248
00:15:27,620 --> 00:15:28,940
It's old and rotten!

249
00:15:30,320 --> 00:15:32,320
